--- !u!114 &31467218
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 31467216}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: f4688fdb7df04437aeb418b961361dc5, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  m_Material: {fileID: 0}
  m_Color: {r: 1, g: 1, b: 1, a: 1}
  m_RaycastTarget: 1
  m_RaycastPadding: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0, w: 0}
  m_Maskable: 1
  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: "                                A simulated, real-time underwater experience.\r\n\n            
    Project: Halley\u2019s Bell harnesses the power of Neural Chips, inserted into
    internally-selected, long-time employees at THC. Operators of the Bell are screened
    for physical condition, eyesight, hearing, proprioception, mental fortitude,
    loyalty, living circumstances, socio-economic status, etc.\r\n\n            
    Compatibility with the Neural Chip must be established in advance. The procedure,
    under the guise of a detailed health screening, is undertaken prior to the formal
    introduction of the Operator to P:HB. The Radio Operator is responsible for overseeing
    the Bell Operator\u2019s descent and has the connection code to the Neural Chip
    on file; they are permitted to close the connection if a threat to P:HB\u2019s
    secrecy is detected at any time. Terminating the connection results in the expiration
    of the Neural Chip, and, in turn, the Operator.\r\n\n             On average,
    previous Operators started experiencing auditory hallucinations at a depth of
    XXXX meters. At about the halfway point, visual aberrations appeared as well.
    Two cases of death by cardiac arrest have been reported. We suspect these effects
    to be a result of the repeated usage of the Inhaler, containing a gaseous compound
    (CO2) beyond human metabolism. The buildup of carbon dioxide in the body decreases
    pH, leading to acidosis and, in turn, organ shutdown. Coupled with the accumulation
    of psychological stress, it is unsurprising that Bell Operator position experiences
    a high turnover rate.\r"
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 109a80438af2a3441b24084aea59b8a4, type: 2}
  m_sharedMaterial: {fileID: -6763452321403479321, guid: 109a80438af2a3441b24084aea59b8a4, type: 2}
  m_fontSharedMaterials: []
  m_fontMaterial: {fileID: 0}
